WEBVTT

00:01.720 --> 00:03.440
That's Lewiston for you!

00:03.840 --> 00:06.900
Since there are so many silver sugar 
masters here, every shop is lovely!

00:07.500 --> 00:08.520
And now...

00:09.220 --> 00:10.840
You're going somewhere else?

00:10.840 --> 00:15.130
Will going to lots of different shops 
cause your scarecrow brain to improve?

00:15.130 --> 00:16.220
How rude.

00:16.220 --> 00:18.140
Since we've come all the way to Lewiston...

00:18.140 --> 00:19.540
just one more shop!

00:24.220 --> 00:24.920
What?

00:26.000 --> 00:27.250
What?

00:27.250 --> 00:28.990
He moved?!

00:28.990 --> 00:29.710
That's right.

00:30.240 --> 00:34.670
Oh, but I really wanted to 
see Alph Hingley's shop.

00:34.670 --> 00:36.540
Alph Hingley?

00:36.540 --> 00:38.180
He's someone I really admire.

00:38.650 --> 00:42.910
People say that his skill rivals that 
of the Silver Sugar Viscount.

00:42.910 --> 00:44.350
Really...

00:47.590 --> 00:50.780
Westol is north of here. 
I wonder if it will be even colder.

00:50.780 --> 00:53.260
If you don't like it, then don't go!

00:53.260 --> 00:54.780
I can't do that.

00:55.230 --> 00:57.800
Since I'm just a sugar artisan 
and not a silver sugar master,

00:57.800 --> 00:59.910
no one here will take any notice of me.

01:00.980 --> 01:05.120
<i>But... in Westol, even I might have a chance.</i>

01:07.230 --> 01:08.080
Oh.

01:08.640 --> 01:10.540
Is this a sugar confectionary, too?

01:11.100 --> 01:14.170
It doesn't have the look of one.

01:14.170 --> 01:15.420
Right?

01:17.680 --> 01:19.760
Say, can we stop inside?

01:19.760 --> 01:21.560
What?!

01:22.760 --> 01:26.100
<i>It seems her scarecrow brain 
is going to improve yet again.</i>

01:27.440 --> 01:35.460
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but…</i>

01:42.160 --> 01:44.880
<i>It's all right</i>

01:44.880 --> 01:48.720
<i>Even alone, I'll be fine, but…</i>

01:48.720 --> 01:55.220
<i>You know, the truth is
 that no one is alone</i>

01:55.220 --> 02:01.800
<i>Things like happiness, 
loneliness, and even anxiety…</i>

02:01.800 --> 02:11.120
<i>We are born to savor all those things</i>

02:11.560 --> 02:14.780
<i>A single spoonful of sparkles</i>

02:14.780 --> 02:17.900
<i>Transforms everything into smiles</i>

02:18.180 --> 02:25.010
<i>That could be what I secretly wished for…</i>

02:25.010 --> 02:27.710
<i>That miracle</i>

02:27.960 --> 02:34.670
<i>We're each searching for
 our most precious treasures</i>

02:34.670 --> 02:40.970
<i>That's what our journey is for</i>

02:40.970 --> 02:48.090
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but...</i>

02:48.090 --> 02:56.320
<i>Each moment that passes before me
 shall be spun from hope</i>

03:01.710 --> 03:03.410
This is incredible.

03:03.790 --> 03:05.950
I wonder who made it.

03:05.950 --> 03:06.870
Hup!

03:07.970 --> 03:10.040
Hey, you. Wake up!

03:10.820 --> 03:13.540
Huh? Who are you?

03:13.540 --> 03:16.660
I am the great Mithril Lid Pod!

03:19.910 --> 03:23.820
Huh? The great Surusuru? Who's that?

03:23.820 --> 03:25.850
You're very easy-going, aren't you?

03:26.800 --> 03:29.680
Now, now. Mithril, you silly.

03:29.680 --> 03:30.460
Huh?

03:32.790 --> 03:33.690
Huh?

03:37.400 --> 03:38.320
What?

03:39.240 --> 03:40.760
Thief!

03:40.760 --> 03:41.570
What?!

03:45.200 --> 03:46.660
What's all that noise?

03:50.200 --> 03:51.580
Oh dear...

03:53.960 --> 03:55.930
What have you done...

03:55.930 --> 03:57.290
you pipsqueak!

03:57.290 --> 03:58.220
What?

04:03.160 --> 04:04.740
Wait, you mean me?!

04:04.740 --> 04:05.970
You have the nerve to play dumb?

04:05.970 --> 04:08.240
Hey, you! Who are you anyway?

04:08.050 --> 04:10.080
Oh, Kat...

04:08.240 --> 04:10.080
You can't just pop out of nowhere like that!

04:10.080 --> 04:11.530
Kat?

04:10.080 --> 04:13.950
The man who just left did this!

04:13.950 --> 04:15.930
Is that true, Benjamin?

04:15.930 --> 04:17.290
Um...

04:17.290 --> 04:21.280
What? He was here! A man in dark clothing!

04:21.280 --> 04:22.780
What is all the commotion?

04:23.630 --> 04:24.610
An argument?

04:24.960 --> 04:27.000
Oh, right. There was.

04:27.000 --> 04:29.180
Someone all in black like him.

04:29.180 --> 04:29.830
What?!

04:32.170 --> 04:34.510
So this fairy fellow is the perpetrator?

04:34.510 --> 04:35.880
What are you speaking of?

04:35.880 --> 04:37.100
No, he isn't!

04:37.100 --> 04:41.270
He's our travel companion, 
and he's only just come into the shop.

04:50.480 --> 04:51.560
You...

04:52.400 --> 04:55.960
Are you that girl who was invited 
before the king at the exhibition?

04:55.960 --> 04:57.690
Oh, um, yes.

04:59.000 --> 05:00.020
Hmm.

05:01.060 --> 05:02.270
Hmm?

05:02.270 --> 05:04.380
All right. Then, work.

05:04.380 --> 05:04.860
What?

05:05.420 --> 05:07.320
Compensate me through labor.

05:07.320 --> 05:09.680
What?! But it wasn't me!

05:09.680 --> 05:12.030
Then, there is no need to work here.

05:12.030 --> 05:12.730
We're leaving.

05:12.730 --> 05:14.460
I'm not letting her go 
until she compensates me.

05:14.460 --> 05:15.910
If you persist, I will cut you down.

05:16.400 --> 05:17.880
Sure, go ahead and try.

05:17.880 --> 05:18.970
I will.

05:18.970 --> 05:19.840
Wait, Challe!

05:19.840 --> 05:21.170
Please, don't do anything dangerous!

05:30.100 --> 05:33.080
Very well. I will work here.

05:33.080 --> 05:35.160
So, please let go, the both of you.

05:35.630 --> 05:36.620
What did you say?

05:36.620 --> 05:37.770
All right!

05:37.770 --> 05:39.660
You can't take that back now!

05:41.730 --> 05:43.260
What are you trying to do?

05:45.650 --> 05:49.140
One sugar confection won't take very long.

05:51.580 --> 05:52.620
And besides...

05:52.620 --> 05:55.420
I want to see how this person works!

05:55.420 --> 05:58.340
How did he make a sugar confection like this?

05:59.390 --> 06:02.020
So, you will make amends 
for something you didn't do?

06:02.020 --> 06:05.260
Yes. It's a good opportunity, 
and I want to learn!

06:05.260 --> 06:09.220
Right, then! You're going to work 
hard for me, you little brat!

06:09.220 --> 06:11.320
Don't go breaking your promise now!

07:03.880 --> 07:05.440
Hurry up, kid.

07:05.440 --> 07:07.570
This sugar confection is needed in two days.

07:07.570 --> 07:09.990
I'm Anne, not "kid," Mister Kat.

07:10.400 --> 07:12.030
Kid is good enough.

07:12.030 --> 07:14.090
And you're the one making fun of me.

07:14.090 --> 07:15.820
I'm not making fun of you.

07:15.820 --> 07:18.450
You're calling me "Mister Cat." 
How is that not making fun of me?

07:18.450 --> 07:21.420
I hate that nickname, and you're 
using it with a "mister"? It's infuriating.

07:21.420 --> 07:23.880
What? Kat is a nickname?

07:23.880 --> 07:27.930
My parents aren't so irresponsible 
that they'd name their son "Kat."

07:29.200 --> 07:33.880
Some idiot gave me that name, and now 
more people know it than my real name.

07:33.880 --> 07:35.550
Hey, Mister Kat.

07:37.470 --> 07:40.080
You have quite the pleasant 
personality, don't you?

07:40.080 --> 07:42.960
You don't have a single sugar 
confection on display in your shop.

07:42.960 --> 07:44.730
Have you any intention of running a business?

07:45.070 --> 07:48.360
Does that sugar confection 
truly have a buyer?

07:49.170 --> 07:52.400
Things are fine as they are. 
I manage to make enough to eat on my own.

07:52.400 --> 07:55.450
And the buyer for this 
is using it for a wedding.

07:55.760 --> 07:58.080
I see. How much is it?

07:58.080 --> 07:58.920
Fifty bayn.

07:58.920 --> 08:00.760
Fifty bayn?!

08:00.760 --> 08:04.250
But why? It should fetch a higher price!

08:04.250 --> 08:07.800
I only make things for people 
I want to make them for.

08:08.270 --> 08:09.110
But...

08:09.550 --> 08:12.220
not all of them can pay a high price.

08:12.960 --> 08:15.840
The person buying this sugar
 confection is a cobbler's daughter.

08:16.620 --> 08:18.850
Even at fifty bayn, it will be 
a difficult purchase for her.

08:22.710 --> 08:26.440
The likelihood that a sugar artisan 
will be an idiot seems quite high.

08:28.820 --> 08:30.480
The silver sugar...

08:31.430 --> 08:32.690
...is all gone, huh?

08:33.150 --> 08:36.880
Because of a certain someone, 
I ended up using more than necessary.

08:36.880 --> 08:41.450
The batch I'm refining will be ready 
by tomorrow morning, but...

08:41.450 --> 08:43.770
Then we have no choice but to wait for it.

08:45.670 --> 08:47.600
Will this be enough?

08:47.600 --> 08:49.130
Yeah, that'll be fine.

08:49.600 --> 08:51.710
Right, then we're done for today.

08:51.710 --> 08:53.500
I'll be counting on you again tomorrow.

09:03.270 --> 09:04.700
<i>The silver sugar...</i>

09:04.700 --> 09:07.450
<i>Will that amount really be enough?</i>

09:25.040 --> 09:26.220
It's so cold.

09:47.200 --> 09:47.810
Oh!

09:51.140 --> 09:52.560
What are you doing?

09:52.560 --> 09:53.900
It's the middle of the night.

09:54.640 --> 09:55.940
Don't startle me like that!

09:55.940 --> 09:57.380
Honestly.

10:00.530 --> 10:02.200
What are you doing?

10:02.200 --> 10:03.710
Did I wake you?

10:03.710 --> 10:04.760
I'm sorry.

10:05.550 --> 10:07.460
You hadn't come back, so I came to see why.

10:07.980 --> 10:10.810
I was thinking of refining another barrel.

10:11.240 --> 10:12.420
Thank you.

10:13.300 --> 10:15.120
Did Kat order you to do this?

10:15.120 --> 10:18.090
No, but I felt like 
we only have barely enough.

10:18.090 --> 10:20.250
It would be disastrous 
if we ran out, wouldn't it?

10:20.250 --> 10:21.190
That's why...

10:23.460 --> 10:25.160
Do you always...

10:25.160 --> 10:27.930
think only of sugar confections?

10:29.810 --> 10:31.860
There's no need to poke fun at me.

10:33.280 --> 10:34.360
Are you cold?

10:34.770 --> 10:35.610
Yes.

10:36.740 --> 10:39.770
Challe, you and the others 
don't feel the cold, is that right?

10:39.770 --> 10:42.060
Yes. I don't understand what it is.

10:42.560 --> 10:43.930
What about warmth?

10:44.710 --> 10:46.060
I feel it a little.

10:46.670 --> 10:49.690
It has a similar feel 
to touching something fluffy.

10:50.270 --> 10:52.360
Something fluffy?

10:54.240 --> 10:56.070
I wonder what that feels like to you.

11:06.650 --> 11:08.810
Ch-Challe... What are you doing?

11:09.440 --> 11:12.120
Doing this makes you feel warmer, doesn't it?

11:12.120 --> 11:14.060
Yes, but...

11:31.150 --> 11:32.680
Thank you, Challe!

11:32.680 --> 11:34.300
I'm all right now.

11:34.810 --> 11:35.850
Are you? Then...

11:51.890 --> 11:53.680
What happened here?

11:53.680 --> 11:55.840
I prepared it, just in case.

11:55.840 --> 11:59.210
The portion that I set out 
to dry yesterday can be milled now,

11:59.210 --> 12:01.020
so we can get to work right away.

12:07.860 --> 12:08.700
Hey.

12:10.320 --> 12:11.930
Did you eat breakfast?

12:12.720 --> 12:13.750
No.

12:13.750 --> 12:15.790
Then go eat first.

12:15.790 --> 12:17.210
An artisan's body is their greatest asset.

12:17.210 --> 12:18.940
Y-Yes, sir!

12:18.940 --> 12:20.510
Benjamin, if you would.

12:20.510 --> 12:21.670
Will do!

13:17.400 --> 13:18.720
Hey, you old hag!

13:18.720 --> 13:20.300
You can't go that way!

13:20.300 --> 13:21.580
It's fine. Now, let me through.

13:21.580 --> 13:22.830
Don't go in there!

13:22.830 --> 13:25.200
It's a sacred workspace!

13:28.360 --> 13:30.830
What brings you here, Viscountess Clay?

13:30.830 --> 13:35.320
I heard that you are making a sugar 
confection for a cobbler's daughter.

13:35.320 --> 13:37.230
I will pay you a hundred cress.

13:37.230 --> 13:38.570
So, just let me have—

13:38.570 --> 13:41.450
I've told you that no matter how often 
you ask, I won't sell anything to you.

13:41.450 --> 13:42.300
What?

13:42.590 --> 13:44.990
You've made things for my servants.

13:44.990 --> 13:46.510
Why not for my daughter?

13:48.600 --> 13:53.230
Try thinking back on how you and 
your daughter treat those servants.

13:53.230 --> 13:55.360
Even if his majesty the king came 
and bowed his head to me,

13:55.360 --> 13:56.720
I won't make anything for you.

13:56.720 --> 13:58.060
I can pay as much as you like.

13:58.060 --> 13:59.440
Go away!

14:02.790 --> 14:04.230
The nerve of a mere artisan...

14:08.580 --> 14:11.940
My, what a beautiful fairy!

14:13.150 --> 14:15.310
Kat, is this your fairy?

14:15.310 --> 14:18.030
I'll pay three hundred cress! Give it to me!

14:18.030 --> 14:19.870
He doesn't belong to anyone!

14:22.470 --> 14:24.480
And who is this girl?

14:24.480 --> 14:26.490
You're an offense to the eyes, you old vixen.

14:26.490 --> 14:27.660
Old vixen?!

14:27.660 --> 14:29.110
Please leave!

14:30.320 --> 14:31.390
Well, I never!

14:31.390 --> 14:32.850
Hooray!

14:32.850 --> 14:35.230
Crap. Forcing her way 
all the way into the workshop...

14:35.230 --> 14:36.660
We need to purify this place! Purify it!

14:39.110 --> 14:39.770
Is that...

14:40.240 --> 14:42.700
Say, Mithril Lid Pod!

14:42.700 --> 14:43.730
Huh?

14:44.190 --> 14:45.800
That scar...

14:46.690 --> 14:49.020
He's the one who smashed 
the sugar confection!

14:49.020 --> 14:51.920
Wow. So, he really does exist.

14:51.920 --> 14:53.660
They don't seem to know when to give up.

14:54.360 --> 14:56.700
<i>I don't ever want to let those two...</i>

14:56.700 --> 14:59.510
<i>touch Kat's sugar confections again.</i>

15:02.150 --> 15:04.020
Somehow, we managed to make it in time.

15:04.440 --> 15:06.280
It truly is beautiful.

15:07.130 --> 15:12.140
I think whoever has this will receive 
the greatest of good luck. I just know it!

15:12.140 --> 15:13.600
That would be nice.

15:13.600 --> 15:16.100
The wedding ceremony is tomorrow. 
Deliver it in the morning.

15:16.380 --> 15:18.240
What? Me?

15:18.240 --> 15:21.060
Go and see the expression 
of the person receiving it.

15:21.360 --> 15:24.020
It's a reward for your 
hard work, you little brat.

15:25.010 --> 15:25.690
Yes, sir!

15:26.080 --> 15:26.920
I'm counting on you!

15:26.920 --> 15:27.930
Yes, sir!

15:27.930 --> 15:30.400
Hey, Benjamin! Heat up the bath!

15:30.400 --> 15:31.620
Will do!

15:31.620 --> 15:32.360
Oh!

15:51.240 --> 15:52.460
That's as far as you'll get!

15:54.990 --> 15:56.260
I <i>knew</i> you would come.

15:59.330 --> 16:00.810
You can't use this route.

16:02.360 --> 16:04.360
Hey. What's all the commotion?

16:04.360 --> 16:05.230
Y-You!

16:05.230 --> 16:07.120
Now that it's come to this...

16:09.300 --> 16:10.530
Don't!

16:14.610 --> 16:17.000
Ow, ow, ow...

16:16.520 --> 16:18.760
Why are you guys...

16:17.000 --> 16:19.100
I'm so dizzy...

16:21.060 --> 16:21.910
So...

16:23.840 --> 16:25.240
Where is the sugar confection?

16:25.240 --> 16:26.750
Where is it?!

16:29.940 --> 16:31.070
I see!

16:31.070 --> 16:33.680
Since the night after we finished 
was the best chance for stealing it...

16:33.680 --> 16:34.600
Yes.

16:34.600 --> 16:37.560
I delivered the sugar 
confection before dinner.

16:37.560 --> 16:40.390
Then I set up the fake and laid in wait.

16:40.810 --> 16:42.380
Who was he?

16:42.380 --> 16:44.440
One of Lady Clay's servants.

16:44.440 --> 16:46.350
The lady probably ordered him to do it.

16:46.720 --> 16:47.870
I see.

16:47.870 --> 16:50.760
So you didn't smash the other one.

16:50.760 --> 16:53.390
I'm sorry. I made you work for nothing.

16:53.390 --> 16:54.360
It's fine!

16:55.020 --> 16:58.450
I learned something incredibly 
important here.

16:59.760 --> 17:03.050
The cobbler's daughter was so happy.

17:03.560 --> 17:08.460
Working here was the tuition 
I paid to be able to see that smile!

17:08.460 --> 17:11.760
Now that I think about it, you're 
heading to Westol after this, aren't you?

17:11.760 --> 17:12.570
Yes.

17:12.570 --> 17:15.400
I'm going to close this place up 
and move south.

17:15.400 --> 17:18.060
I've gotten sick of Lewiston's winters.

17:18.060 --> 17:21.180
Well, you are a cat. 
They don't tolerate the cold well.

17:21.610 --> 17:24.890
Do you get some benefit 
out of saying mean things to me?

17:25.440 --> 17:26.720
It improves my mood.

17:26.720 --> 17:29.720
Your personality is <i>incredibly</i> twisted.

17:29.720 --> 17:30.720
Hey, Benjamin!

17:30.720 --> 17:32.360
Yeah?

17:34.860 --> 17:36.380
You can have my winter clothes.

17:36.380 --> 17:39.120
What? I couldn't possibly accept 
something so extravagant!

17:39.120 --> 17:40.400
Moron.

17:40.400 --> 17:42.790
You're a kid, so just be happy 
like a kid should be.

17:43.920 --> 17:45.530
It's lovely.

17:45.530 --> 17:48.880
But something so lovely won't suit me at all.

17:49.340 --> 17:52.650
Anne, in another five years, 
you'll be able to wear it with style!

17:52.650 --> 17:54.540
I can't imagine that.

17:54.540 --> 17:55.950
It will happen!

17:55.950 --> 17:58.670
Anne, you're going to get 
even cuter from here!

17:58.670 --> 18:02.280
What's this? You've got a good eye!

18:02.280 --> 18:02.810
Oh.

18:02.810 --> 18:04.390
We can't give you this.

18:04.390 --> 18:05.350
Oh.

18:05.350 --> 18:06.620
That pouch?

18:06.620 --> 18:07.360
Yeah.

18:07.360 --> 18:09.440
It's got my wing in it.

18:09.440 --> 18:11.400
What? What do you mean?

18:11.400 --> 18:15.770
Kat always puts my wing 
somewhere and forgets about it.

18:16.280 --> 18:20.110
That's why I put it in here. 
So it wouldn't get lost.

18:20.110 --> 18:23.120
So Kat doesn't keep your wing with him?

18:23.120 --> 18:24.740
He forgets.

18:25.050 --> 18:28.990
He's indifferent about everything 
but sugar confections.

18:28.990 --> 18:31.550
Huh? But then, can't you run away?

18:31.550 --> 18:33.520
If I wanted to.

18:34.000 --> 18:35.020
But...

18:35.420 --> 18:37.980
I've seen lots of humans,

18:37.980 --> 18:42.160
but watching Kat is fun, so I like it here.

18:42.160 --> 18:42.890
Say...

18:43.450 --> 18:47.300
You've lived a really long time,
 haven't you, Benjamin?

18:47.710 --> 18:49.260
Well...

18:49.750 --> 18:54.060
I counted up to 250 years, but...

18:56.260 --> 18:58.140
Thank you for everything!

18:58.140 --> 19:01.320
Oh, right. Do you know 
the Silver Sugar Viscount?

19:01.320 --> 19:02.250
What?

19:02.650 --> 19:04.910
If you go to Westol, you may run into him.

19:05.230 --> 19:06.120
What?

19:06.120 --> 19:08.400
Kat, you know Hugh, too?

19:08.400 --> 19:09.470
Yeah.

19:09.470 --> 19:12.730
I trained with that guy 
at the Mercury Workshop.

19:12.730 --> 19:16.730
After I became a silver sugar master, 
I got sick of it and left the school, though.

19:16.730 --> 19:17.630
What?!

19:17.630 --> 19:20.170
Kat, you've received the royal medal?!

19:20.170 --> 19:22.940
Huh? Your head really is empty, isn't it?

19:22.940 --> 19:27.680
But, I mean, there's no one named Kat 
among this town's silver sugar masters.

19:27.680 --> 19:31.550
Honestly. I told you, Kat is a nickname!

19:31.550 --> 19:34.680
And it was that dimwitted 
reprobate who gave it to me.

19:35.180 --> 19:37.110
My name is Alph Hingley.

19:37.110 --> 19:40.570
What?!

19:40.570 --> 19:42.160
He moved?!

19:42.160 --> 19:43.000
That's right.

19:44.310 --> 19:48.380
Oh, but I really wanted 
to see Alph Hingley's shop.

19:48.380 --> 19:49.790
Alph Hingley?

19:49.790 --> 19:51.450
He's someone I really admire.

19:51.450 --> 19:53.540
<i>Kat is </i>that<i> Hingley?</i>

19:53.540 --> 19:56.500
So, when he said you're moving, 
he meant in the future?

19:57.670 --> 19:58.480
What is it?

19:58.480 --> 20:03.470
I'm just thinking about the fact that someone 
I admire has been calling me a little brat.

20:04.210 --> 20:05.380
Admire?

20:06.860 --> 20:10.390
If you're an artisan, too, 
then don't look up to anyone else.

20:10.960 --> 20:13.850
You are one of a kind. 
And second to <i>absolutely</i> no one.

20:22.150 --> 20:24.940
<i>I feel like Hugh said 
something similar to me, too.</i>

20:25.750 --> 20:28.240
<i>He said I shouldn't ape anyone else.</i>

20:28.930 --> 20:30.890
<i>Thank you, Kat.</i>

20:30.890 --> 20:32.120
<i>Farewell!</i>

20:33.040 --> 20:35.050
<i>I'll work hard in Westol, too!</i>

20:37.900 --> 20:40.630
Would you like a sugar confection?

20:40.910 --> 20:43.590
I can create to your tastes!

20:44.060 --> 20:47.070
Would you like a sugar confection?

20:44.530 --> 20:47.070
Weren't your chances 
supposed to be better in Westol?

20:47.070 --> 20:48.510
Hey! Challe fenn Challe!

20:48.510 --> 20:50.090
Just because not a single piece has sold,

20:50.090 --> 20:53.240
doesn't mean you get to talk like 
Anne's completely misread things! <i>Got it</i>?

20:58.500 --> 21:00.440
It's cold again today, isn't it?

20:59.250 --> 21:04.990
Anne and the Cat's Sugar Confectionary

21:16.250 --> 21:20.580
<i>Is it just like the dreams we dream at night?</i>

21:21.450 --> 21:26.720
<i>Do we give names to our other dreams because,</i>

21:26.720 --> 21:30.260
<i>Just as our night dreams are forgotten upon waking,</i>

21:30.260 --> 21:37.330
<i>If they aren't held dear, they will disappear?</i>

21:37.330 --> 21:48.470
<i>No, it's because they aren't things that only special people can see</i>

21:48.470 --> 21:49.200
<i>That day</i>

21:49.200 --> 21:53.650
<i>I reached out again and again</i>

21:53.650 --> 21:59.210
<i>I failed to catch that shining fruit, and yet</i>

21:59.210 --> 22:04.710
<i>I'll reach out once more</i>

22:04.710 --> 22:09.010
<i>If I make my wishes come true myself</i>

22:09.010 --> 22:14.840
<i>I just know it will make you smile</i>

22:14.840 --> 22:26.320
<i>That's why I'm able to say I'm not giving up</i>

22:36.080 --> 22:40.040
<b>The Castle on the Sea</b>
